WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.424 --> 00:00:07.646
The sun rose, and the children were no longer statues.

2
00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:11.909
They were standing knee-deep in brambles and grass.

3
00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:17.532
The lawn, the marble steps, and the pool had disappeared.

4
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.441
It was very cold.

5
00:00:35.461 --> 00:00:38.723
"We're on the island," said Mabel.

6
00:00:38.743 --> 00:00:41.385
"But we can't swim anymore.

7
00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:42.866
We're stuck here."

8
00:00:42.886 --> 00:00:46.628
"Isn't there a boat somewhere?"

9
00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:47.909
Jimmy asked.

10
00:00:50.691 --> 00:00:52.652
"No." Mabel shivered.

11
00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:57.475
"There must be something we can do," said Gerald.

12
00:00:57.495 --> 00:00:59.857
"The ring!"

13
00:01:00.277 --> 00:01:01.018
cried Mabel.

14
00:01:01.038 --> 00:01:04.000
"We can wish ourselves home.

15
00:01:04.376 --> 00:01:05.797
Do you have the ring, Kathleen?"

16
00:01:07.397 --> 00:01:08.778
Kathleen shook her head.

17
00:01:08.798 --> 00:01:13.240
"Psyche wanted to see it so I gave it to her.

18
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.621
It's probably still on her finger!"

19
00:01:19.242 --> 00:01:22.204
Everyone tried not to be angry with Kathleen.

20
00:01:22.864 --> 00:01:24.425
But everyone was upset.

21
00:01:28.086 --> 00:01:31.988
we can find Psyche's statue and get the ring back," said Gerald.

22
00:01:33.712 --> 00:01:36.634
"I've never seen that statue," said Mabel.

23
00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:38.795
Kathleen sniffled.

24
00:01:40.796 --> 00:01:42.037
She was about to cry.

25
00:01:42.057 --> 00:01:46.399
"Why don't we explore the island," said Gerald.

26
00:01:46.419 --> 00:01:48.780
"Maybe we'll find a boat."

27
00:01:52.042 --> 00:01:54.343
None of them believed that they'd find a boat.

28
00:01:56.505 --> 00:01:58.886
But they set off to explore the island anyway.

29
00:02:00.907 --> 00:02:02.508
They were all miserable.

30
00:02:03.676 --> 00:02:06.599
The brambles scratched Mabel's bare feet and legs.

31
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.442
She had left her shoes and stockings on the mainland.

32
00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:14.745
"Come on, everybody, cheer up," said Gerald.

33
00:02:14.765 --> 00:02:16.907
"We'll get out of here."

34
00:02:18.669 --> 00:02:21.851
Suddenly he stumbled and disappeared with a yell.

35
00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:24.934
Mabel nearly fell too.

36
00:02:26.535 --> 00:02:29.798
Right in front of her was a flight of moss-covered steps.

37
00:02:29.818 --> 00:02:33.529
"Gerald, are you hurt?"

38
00:02:34.029 --> 00:02:35.331
she called down the steps.

39
00:02:35.351 --> 00:02:38.614
"A little," he said.

40
00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.396
"But I found a passage."

41
00:02:43.298 --> 00:02:46.841
"There's always a passage in this place," said Jimmy.

42
00:02:46.861 --> 00:02:51.085
"I forgot about that passage!"

43
00:02:51.486 --> 00:02:52.386
declared Mabel.

44
00:02:52.407 --> 00:02:57.972
"It goes under the water and comes out at the Temple of Flora!

45
00:02:59.836 --> 00:03:03.997
Maybe it even goes past the place where the Ugly-Wugly found his good hotel."

46
00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:09.199
"I'm not going down there in the dark," said Kathleen.

47
00:03:10.779 --> 00:03:12.520
Gerald came back up the steps.

48
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.560
"Maybe there's a secret spring."

49
00:03:17.561 --> 00:03:19.882
Then Gerald led the way down the steps.

50
00:03:22.622 --> 00:03:25.563
He held Kathleen's hand so she wouldn't feel afraid.

51
00:03:27.103 --> 00:03:30.001
The steps led to a passage, which took a turn.

52
00:03:31.482 --> 00:03:32.803
Then there were more steps.

53
00:03:33.804 --> 00:03:37.087
These led to a straight, clean, marble passage.

54
00:03:39.429 --> 00:03:42.931
Suddenly the children found themselves in a great hall.

55
00:03:43.972 --> 00:03:45.574
The room was filled with light.

56
00:03:46.594 --> 00:03:50.277
And each one of them noticed something different in the arches around the room.

57
00:03:51.278 --> 00:03:52.699
There was a ship at sea.

58
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.361
A king on his throne.

59
00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:57.924
The Ugly-Wugly sitting happily in front of a good hotel.

60
00:04:00.496 --> 00:04:01.777
"Oh, I'm glad we came!"

61
00:04:02.257 --> 00:04:03.098
said Kathleen.

62
00:04:05.139 --> 00:04:07.040
They walked slowly through the hall.

63
00:04:08.541 --> 00:04:13.724
At the end of the hall, they saw the source of the light: the statue of Psyche.

64
00:04:14.904 --> 00:04:16.665
On its hand was the ring.

65
00:04:20.888 --> 00:04:23.789
hope you don't mind," Gerald said to the statue.

66
00:04:25.651 --> 00:04:27.912
He removed the ring very gently.

67
00:04:30.684 --> 00:04:34.486
They passed Psyche and entered a dark, twisting passage.

68
00:04:34.506 --> 00:04:39.589
"Give me the ring, Gerald," said Kathleen.

69
00:04:39.609 --> 00:04:41.510
"I know what to say."

70
00:04:43.251 --> 00:04:45.533
Gerald handed it to her reluctantly.

71
00:04:49.275 --> 00:04:54.558
wish," she said slowly, "that no one at home will know we've been out tonight.

72
00:04:55.158 --> 00:04:58.180
I wish we were safe in our own beds and asleep."

73
00:05:02.546 --> 00:05:05.322
And that is exactly what happened next.
